Tark: a CRLSet in every release (tarka-notes 2026-10-22-trust-data-updates).

Tark's component updater fetches only Widevine, so Chrome's CRLSet never
reached it: Chrome blocked the compromised eMudhra intermediates within
hours on 17 October 2026, and Tark needed a hand-made release. Each release
now carries the CRLSet Chrome had when it was made, which
utils/trust_data.py fetches from the CRLSet component, checks against the
key Chromium pins for it, and writes as tark_crl_set_data.inc. It is handed
to the certificate verifier at startup, before any page loads. The verifier
keeps the CRLSet with the higher sequence number, so a newer one delivered
later wins and this one never replaces a newer one. The verifier parses
CRLSets at USER_VISIBLE priority instead of BEST_EFFORT: BEST_EFFORT tasks
wait until startup is over, and pages loaded in the first seconds (a
restored session) were verified without the CRLSet.

The CT log list and the Chrome Root Store come the same way, but need no
code: trust_data.py install writes them over Chromium's files.

